laurel 2784: camera: where the signal stops. New laurel_cam_light.h (pure, host-tested) + laurel_cam_light.c: rails line (rail pins' control and in/out words, PM6125 L12A enable, mV, mode, status read from the PMIC, which LDOs are on), read-back of the sensor registers that decide the picture + temperature sensor at the boot self-check and at frame 6 of a session, every value of the init + mode tables read back once a boot in standby, the sensor's own colour bars (0x0601 = 2, the library's test_pattern_info) in memory for 150 ms once a boot before the real frames, statistics straight from the raw bytes (min, max, top 3 bits, Bayer places, 5-byte group) at the boot, at frame 6 and every 150 frames of a session. Stock difference fixed: L12A gets the high power mode vote (lsmd 7) the stock 80 mA load gives; the mode goes back to 4 at power-off. The kernel's "1% over" has one-step bins under 32. SPMI user "camera". Nothing else changes for the frames; a failed read only gives a line. docs/laurel_sprout/camera.md section 12.

